  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[6]{11-5x}-1.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the roots of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{11-5x}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{11-5x}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{11-5x} & =1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[6]{11-5x})^{6} & ={1}^{6} \\\\ 11-5x & =1 \\\\ -5x & =-10 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{11-5\\cdot 2}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{1}-1 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=2.$",
